# Byte offsets into spine/pages.jsonl are computed at build time and used by
# the browser as HTTP Range requests against the copy GitHub Pages serves.
# With core.autocrlf the working tree gained one \r per line, so every offset
# after the first was short by the number of preceding lines and every page
# transcript but the first failed to parse. The indexed bytes and the served
# bytes have to be the same bytes, so git must never rewrite line endings here.
* -text
